@startuml

' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
'  CloudAI — Worker Failure & Task Requeue Sequence
'  Designed for 16:9 slides · Same visual language as main lifecycle diagram
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 20
skinparam roundCorner 8

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #1E293B
    ArrowFontSize 20
    ArrowFontColor #1E293B
    LifeLineBorderColor #1E293B
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #94A3B8
    LifeLineBorderThickness 3
    ParticipantBorderThickness 2
    ParticipantBorderColor #1E3A5F
    ParticipantFontSize 28
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    ParticipantPadding 40
    DividerBorderColor #64748B
    DividerBorderThickness 2
    DividerFontColor #0F172A
    DividerFontSize 24
    GroupBorderColor #64748B
    GroupHeaderFontSize 20
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

skinparam note {
    BorderColor #94A3B8
    BackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    FontSize 18
    FontColor #1E293B
}

title <size:36><b>CloudAI — Worker Failure & Task Requeue</b></size>\n<size:18><color:#475569>Heartbeat timeout  ·  Recovery  ·  Re-scheduling  ·  Late results</color></size>\n

participant "    Master Node    " as M #B6D4F7
participant "    PPO Service    " as P #D4C8F5
participant "   Worker A   \n<size:14><color:#991B1B>fails mid-task</color></size>" as WA #F6B8B8
participant "   Worker B   \n<size:14><color:#166534>takes over</color></size>" as WB #A7EDCA

|||

== <b>  Task Running on Worker A  </b> ==

activate WA #F6B8B8
M -> WA : **AssignTask**(task, attempt_1)
WA --> M : Ack ✓
WA -> WA : Pull → Create → Run container

loop <size:16>Heartbeats — every 5 s</size>
    WA -> M : SendHeartbeat(running_tasks)
end

WA ->x] : ❌  **Worker A crashes / loses network**
note right of WA #FECACA : Container orphaned\nHeartbeats stop

deactivate WA

|||

== <b>  Failure Detection  </b> ==

activate M #B6D4F7
M -> M : checkAndMarkInactiveWorkers()\n**> 30 s** since last heartbeat
note right of M #FDEAAB : DB: Worker A → **inactive**

|||

== <b>  Task Recovery  </b> ==

M -> M : recoverWorkerTasksLocked()
note right of M #FDEAAB : DB: ATTEMPT_1 → **lost**\nRelease CPU / mem / storage\nDelete ASSIGNMENT\nTASK → **queued** (recovery +1)
M -> M : enqueueRecoveredTask()
note right of M #D1FAE5 : Task re-enters\nscheduling queue

|||

== <b>  Re-scheduling to Worker B  </b> ==

M -> P : **SelectWorker**(task, candidates)
P --> M : Worker B selected
note right of P #D4C8F5 : Worker A excluded\n(marked inactive)
M -> WB : **AssignTask**(task, attempt_2)
WB --> M : Ack ✓
note right of M #FDEAAB : DB: new ATTEMPT_2 created\nTASK → **running**
deactivate M

|||

== <b>  Successful Execution on Worker B  </b> ==

activate WB #A7EDCA
WB -> WB : Pull → Create → Run container
WB -> WB : Container exits → Collect outputs
deactivate WB

WB -> M : **ReportCompletion**(success, logs, files)
note right of M #FDEAAB : DB: ATTEMPT_2 → **completed**\nStore RESULT · Release resources

|||

== <b>  Late Result from Worker A  </b> ==

WA -->> M : **ReportCompletion**(attempt_1, …)
note right of M #FECACA : attempt_1 ≠ current attempt_2\nATTEMPT_1 → **stale**\nResult stored for audit\n**Ignored** — not terminal

|||

@enduml
